// Rust → TypeScript interop: replay `server-rs/crates/rh-proto/vectors/rust.json`,
// generated by the agent's crate, through the browser implementation on
// node's WebCrypto.
//
// What these pin: every hub and mux frame encodes to the same bytes; the mux
// scheduler emits the same frames in the same order; given the same keys and
// ephemerals the WebCrypto Noise IK writes exactly what `snow` wrote, reads
// `snow`'s replies, and stays in step through rekeys by count and by age; a
// Rust-signed device chain verifies (and every chain Rust refuses is refused
// here with the same error), with its recovery key's proof and its committed
// key epochs; Rust-sealed records open and tampering is caught;
// Rust-wrapped keys unwrap into non-extractable keys; and the key checks
// (weak Ed25519 encodings, low-order X25519 keys, non-canonical signatures)
// agree.
